      "id": 1,
      "text": "Civic Center earned National Historic Landmark status in 1987 and joined the National Register of Historic Places in 1978.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Civic_Center%2C_San_Francisco",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "An illuminated archway graced Civic Center Plaza in 1925 to celebrate the city's Diamond Jubilee.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://sfciviccenter.org/history/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The United Nations Charter was signed in the Veterans Building's Herbst Theatre in 1945, sparking the UN's birth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Civic_Center%2C_San_Francisco",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1951, the Treaty of San Francisco ended the Pacific War and was signed within Civic Center.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Civic_Center%2C_San_Francisco",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Pioneer Monument, funded by James Lick, honors Manifest Destiny and sits on Fulton Street between the Library and Asian Art Museum.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Civic_Center%2C_San_Francisco",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Civic Center’s original plan called for City Hall, Auditorium, Main Library, Opera House, and State Office Building facing a central plaza.",
